  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A singly ionized magnesium atom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;ion is accelerated to kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>keV</mi></math>, and is projected perpendicularly into a magnetic field $B$ of the magnitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The radius of path formed will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The radius of circle formed by a charged particle in a magnetic field perpendicular to the velocity is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>5000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup></mstyle></msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>979</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>",
